MARKETING PLAN Q1 2027 - Recycled-polyester backpack range
Owner: Accessories marketing
Product: Recycled-polyester backpack range (Backpacks, style STY-9509: SKU-106363 Black, SKU-106370 Navy, SKU-106377 Sage), three core colours plus one premium laptop-sleeve style
Launch date: 12 January 2027
Total marketing budget: £250k
Target audience: 18-35 commuters and students, UK online and stores
Price positioning: core backpack £33.99, laptop style £44.99, positioned mid-market below premium outdoor brands (£60-£90) and above value high-street bags (£15-£25)
Planned first-buy: 18000 units across DCs and top 60 stores

| week_from_launch | activity | spend_gbp | expected_effect |
| -4 to -1 | teaser email, paid social, influencer seeding | 45000 | build waitlist of 40,000 sign-ups |
| 1 | launch email, homepage takeover, paid social | 60000 | launch spike in weeks 1-2 |
| 2 | retargeting and PR sponsored posts | 25000 | sustain launch demand |
| 3 | influencer burst (12 creators) and student offer | 55000 | second peak in week 3-4 |
| 4 to 8 | always-on paid social and search | 40000 | steady state |
| 9 to 12 | spring commuter campaign | 25000 | modest lift in weeks 9-12 |

Expected market reach: 500,000 impressions per week in launch weeks 1-4
Success measures: week 1 sell-through 8%, week 3 sell-through 20%, online conversion 3.2%
Risks: influencer content slips by a week; paid social costs rise in January
